# Implementation Plan - Global Header Strategy

## Goal
Implement a consistent, "Soulful" header across the application that handles greetings ("Ayubowan"), context (School/Role), and navigation requirements, while replacing inconsistent per-screen headers.

## Conflict Mitigation Strategy
> [!IMPORTANT]
> To avoid merge conflicts with other developers, we will use a **"Component-First, Integrate-Later"** approach.
> 1.  **Phase 1**: Build [GlobalHeader](file:///C:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/components/shared/GlobalHeader.tsx#28-118) as a generic component. (Touches 0 existing files).
> 2.  **Phase 2**: Integrate into **one** screen ([ClassroomScreen](file:///C:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/screens/ClassroomScreen.tsx#30-101)) to test. (Touches 1 file).
> 3.  **Phase 3**: Roll out to other screens one by one.

## Proposed Changes

### Components [NEW]
#### [NEW] [GlobalHeader.tsx](file:///C:/Users/Naween/projects/polymath-platform/apps/gurudevi-mobile/src/components/shared/GlobalHeader.tsx)
-   **Purpose**: A reusable header component.
-   **Props**:
    -   `title`: string (optional, overrides default)
    -   `showGreeting`: boolean (for Home/Dashboard)
    -   `rightAction`: ReactNode (optional, for settings/filter icons)
    -   `backButton`: boolean (default false)
-   **Features**:
    -   Displays "Ayubowan, [Name]" if `showGreeting` is true.
    -   Displays School Name/Role as subtitle.
    -   Uses `Theme.colors.voidIndigo` background to blend with screens.

